IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`
IMPORT `er3-earnings`

-- Tests of er3-earnings (regulation 35). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of
-- reg 35 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 541-605), beside the assertion, before the module was run.
-- Naming: `test ...` names are local to this file and are never imported.

`test purpose 14(2)` MEANS `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations`
`test purpose 14 other` MEANS `er3 purpose: an interruption of earnings under section 14 of the Regulations, other than subsection (2)`
`test purpose deduction` MEANS `er3 purpose: the amount to be deducted from benefits`
`test purpose 45-46` MEANS `er3 purpose: sections 45 and 46 of the Act`

`test fact employment` MEANS `er3 income: arising out of any employment`
`test fact bankrupt` MEANS `er3 income: payable in respect of wages, benefits or other remuneration from the proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt employer`
`test fact WC` MEANS `er3 income: a workers' compensation payment received or to be received`
`test fact WC lump` MEANS `er3 income: a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments`
`test fact disability pension` MEANS `er3 income: a disability pension`
`test fact sickness plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`
`test fact not group` MEANS `er3 income: that plan is not a group plan under subsection (8)`
`test fact sick leave plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan`
`test fact child leave plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act`
`test fact family leave plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act`
`test fact ill child plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child`
`test fact ill adult plan` MEANS `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult`
`test fact motor vehicle` MEANS `er3 income: a payment from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan provided under a provincial law in respect of the actual or presumed loss of income from employment due to injury`
`test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted` MEANS `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received from that motor vehicle plan`
`test fact pension moneys` MEANS `er3 income: moneys paid or payable on account of or in lieu of a pension`
`test fact provincial indemnity` MEANS `er3 income: an indemnity payment under a provincial law because the claimant ceased to work as continuation of work entailed physical dangers`
`test fact provincial benefits not counted` MEANS `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received under that provincial law`
`test fact hours after injury` MEANS `er3 income: after the week of the injury the claimant accumulated the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act`
`test fact injured before 152.08` MEANS `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person who sustained the injury before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act`
`test fact lay-off pay` MEANS `er3 income: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`
`test fact allowance not deducted` MEANS `er3 income: an allowance that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Act`
`test fact relief grants` MEANS `er3 income: relief grants in cash or in kind`
`test fact retroactive increase` MEANS `er3 income: a retroactive increase in wages or salary`
`test fact self-employed` MEANS `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person`
`test fact payable before 152.08` MEANS `er3 income: the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act`
`test fact hours after payable` MEANS `er3 income: the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the benefit period were accumulated after the moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they were received`
`test fact ITA 6(16)` MEANS `er3 income: employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act`

§ `reg 35(1) -- the definitions`

-- "employment" is any one of the three limbs.
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- "income": pecuniary or non-pecuniary, AND received or to be received from an employer or any other person.
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) income` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) income` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) income` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) income` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- "pension": a retirement pension arising from one of three sources.
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(1) pension` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `reg 35(2) -- the earnings to be taken into account`

-- Ordinary wages from an employment are earnings for all four purposes.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`) `test purpose 45-46` EQUALS TRUE

-- Income that does not arise out of an employment and is in none of (a) to (f) is not earnings.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` EMPTY `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE

-- (a) payments from the proceeds of a bankrupt employer's property are brought in.
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(a) amounts payable from the proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt employer` (LIST `test fact bankrupt`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact bankrupt`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE

-- (b) workers' compensation payments; a lump sum or pension in full and final settlement is not.
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(b) workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement` (LIST `test fact WC`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(b) workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement` (LIST `test fact WC`, `test fact WC lump`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact WC`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact WC`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS TRUE
-- (4): not for the purpose of subsection 14(2).
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact WC`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS FALSE
-- (7)(a): the lump sum of final settlement is not earnings for any purpose.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact WC lump`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact disability pension`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE

-- (c)(i) a group wage-loss indemnity plan: a sickness or disability plan that is not "not a group plan".
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`, `test fact not group`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
-- (4): a group sickness or disability payment is not earnings for subsection 14(2) only.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS TRUE
-- (7)(b): a payment under a plan that is not a group plan is not earnings for any purpose.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`, `test fact not group`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sickness plan`, `test fact not group`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS FALSE

-- (c)(ii) to (vi): each leave plan is within (c).
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact sick leave plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact child leave plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact family leave plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact ill child plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(c) payments under a group wage-loss indemnity plan or one of the leave plans` (LIST `test fact ill adult plan`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact sick leave plan`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS TRUE

-- (d) motor vehicle accident insurance payments, only if the benefits under the Act are not taken into account.
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`, `test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(d) payments from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`, `test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
-- (3): the injury week was followed by the hours required by section 7 or 7.1.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`, `test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted`, `test fact hours after injury`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
-- (3.1): a self-employed person injured before the period of section 152.08.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`, `test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted`, `test fact injured before 152.08`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
-- (3) and (3.1) take out only a payment within (2)(d): other income is untouched.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact hours after injury`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
-- "notwithstanding paragraph (7)(b)": a motor vehicle payment from a non-group plan stays earnings.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact motor vehicle`, `test fact motor vehicle benefits not counted`, `test fact sickness plan`, `test fact not group`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE

-- (e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension.
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(e) moneys paid on account of or in lieu of a pension` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`) `test purpose 45-46` EQUALS TRUE
-- (5): not earnings for the purposes of section 14 (both 14(2) and the rest of section 14).
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS FALSE
-- (7)(e)(i): a self-employed person's moneys that became payable before the 152.08 period.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact self-employed`, `test fact payable before 152.08`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
-- a self-employed person's moneys that did not become payable before: still earnings.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact self-employed`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
-- the (ii) fact does not help a self-employed person: only (i) is for them.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact self-employed`, `test fact hours after payable`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
-- (7)(e)(ii): another claimant whose hours were accumulated after the moneys became payable.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact hours after payable`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
-- the (i) fact does not help another claimant: only (ii) is for them.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact pension moneys`, `test fact payable before 152.08`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE

-- (f) indemnity payments under a provincial law because continuing to work entailed physical dangers.
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(f) indemnity payments under a provincial law because continuing to work entailed physical dangers` (LIST `test fact provincial indemnity`, `test fact provincial benefits not counted`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(2)(f) indemnity payments under a provincial law because continuing to work entailed physical dangers` (LIST `test fact provincial indemnity`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact provincial indemnity`, `test fact provincial benefits not counted`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact provincial indemnity`, `test fact provincial benefits not counted`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS TRUE
-- (4): not for subsection 14(2).
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact provincial indemnity`, `test fact provincial benefits not counted`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS FALSE

§ `reg 35(6), (7) -- income that is not earnings`

-- (6): lay-off or separation earnings and allowances not deducted under 16(1) are not earnings for section 14 only.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact lay-off pay`) `test purpose 14(2)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact lay-off pay`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact lay-off pay`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact allowance not deducted`) `test purpose 14 other` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact allowance not deducted`) `test purpose 45-46` EQUALS TRUE

-- (7)(c), (d), (f): never earnings, whatever else is true of the income.
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact relief grants`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact retroactive increase`) `test purpose deduction` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` (LIST `test fact employment`, `test fact ITA 6(16)`) `test purpose 45-46` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(7) the portion of the income derived from an excluded source is not earnings` (LIST `test fact employment`) EQUALS FALSE

§ `reg 35(8), (9) -- a plan that is not a group plan`

-- (9) portable: both the benefits and the premium rate stay equivalent.
#ASSERT `reg 35(9) portable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(9) portable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(9) portable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- (8) all six features: a plan that is not related to a single employer's group, not financed by an employer,
-- voluntarily purchased, completely portable, constant benefits, premium independent of group experience.
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- each feature missing in turn makes it a group plan.
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `reg 35(10) to (16) -- the value of the income`

-- (10)(a): 10000 received, less 1500 of expenses, less 500 of consideration supplied = 8000.
#ASSERT `reg 35(10)(a) to (c) the income from the employment` `er3 claimant who is not self-employed` 10000 1500 500 0 0 0 EQUALS 8000
-- (10)(b): farming: 20000 gross plus 3000 of subsidies, less 5000 of operating expenses = 18000.
#ASSERT `reg 35(10)(a) to (c) the income from the employment` `er3 claimant who is self-employed in farming` 0 0 0 20000 3000 5000 EQUALS 18000
-- (10)(c): other self-employment: 15000 gross less 4000 of operating expenses = 11000; subsidies are not counted.
#ASSERT `reg 35(10)(a) to (c) the income from the employment` `er3 claimant who is self-employed in employment other than farming` 0 0 0 15000 999 4000 EQUALS 11000

-- (10)(d): the value of board, living quarters and other benefits is added; unknown value: not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 35(10) the income taken into account, with the value of board, living quarters and other benefits` 8000 (JUST 1200) EQUALS JUST 9200
#ASSERT `reg 35(10) the income taken into account, with the value of board, living quarters and other benefits` 8000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (11), (12): the agreed value if reasonable; otherwise the Commission's.
#ASSERT `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` TRUE 1200 TRUE (JUST 900) EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` TRUE 1200 FALSE (JUST 900) EQUALS JUST 900
#ASSERT `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` FALSE 0 FALSE (JUST 700) EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` TRUE 1200 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (13): rooms 400 plus heat, light and telephone 150 = 550.
#ASSERT `reg 35(13) the value of living quarters` 400 150 EQUALS 550
-- (14): the rental value of similar quarters in the same district.
#ASSERT `reg 35(14) the value of living quarters determined by the Commission` 650 EQUALS 650
-- (15): the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration, only when the conditions hold.
#ASSERT `reg 35(15) the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration to be included in the income` TRUE TRUE 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `reg 35(15) the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration to be included in the income` TRUE FALSE 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 35(15) the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration to be included in the income` FALSE TRUE 300 EQUALS 0
-- (16): living quarters are rooms or any other living accommodation.
#ASSERT `reg 35(16) living quarters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(16) living quarters` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 35(16) living quarters` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
